┌─ Summary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                            │
│  Formalization of bounded integer compositions and their (un)ranking       │
│  algorithms in Lean.                                                       │
│                                                                            │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─ Prerequisites ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                            │
│  GNU `make` and Lean's Lake are required. Lean 4.28.0 and Mathlib v4.28.0  │
│  are pinned in `lean-toolchain` and `lake-manifest.json`.                  │
│                                                                            │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─ Usage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                            │
│  Type `make` to build the library.                                         │
│                                                                            │
│  Import `GenericRankingBic`, or individual modules. `CountingContract`     │
│  supplies counts; `Strategy` supplies decomposition, traversal and rank    │
│  arithmetic. The generic inverse proofs are `rank_unrank` and              │
│  `unrank_rank`.                                                            │
│                                                                            │
│  The examples in `GenericRankingBic.lean` show the counting                │
│  implementations and paper strategies.                                     │
│                                                                            │
│  The source modules are grouped into `Counting`, `Orders`, `Ranking` and   │
│  `Tables`.                                                                 │
│                                                                            │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─ Verification ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                            │
│  Type `make check` to build all sources and inspect the library proofs'    │
│  axiom dependencies. The permitted axioms are `propext`,                   │
│  `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`. `ProofAudit` is a separate           │
│  verification library in the same Lake package.                            │
│                                                                            │
│  Type `make comparator` to compare the statements in                       │
│  `ProofAudit/Challenge.lean` with the proofs in                            │
│  `ProofAudit/Solution.lean`. It needs `comparator`, `lean4export` and      │
│  `landrun`. The fixtures share the library definitions.                    │
│                                                                            │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
